paragraph.content:
coordinate with the Secretary of State to support international efforts on marine and freshwater
 harmful algal bloom and hypoxia information sharing, research, prediction,
 mitigation, control, and response activities;

facilitate and provide resources to train State and local coastal and water resource managers in
 the methods and technologies for monitoring, preventing, controlling, and
 mitigating marine and freshwater harmful algal blooms and hypoxia;

mechanisms, including the potential costs and benefits of those mechanisms, to protect ecosystems
 that may be or have been affected by harmful algal bloom and hypoxia
 events;

assess the progress made toward nutrient load reductions, the response of the hypoxic zone and
 water quality throughout the Mississippi/Atchafalaya River Basin, and the
 economic and social effects;
